diff --git a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
index d4b10f0..fff5464 100644
--- a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
+++ b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -194,6 +194,7 @@ Renderer code never executes kubectl directly; it only communicates with the pre
 - Each container's mount list renders inside a native `<details>`/`<summary>` element labeled "Mounts (n)", collapsed by default, rather than a custom accordion component — native disclosure widgets give free keyboard/accessibility support and need no extra state.
 - `PodDetailsOverlay` is resizable: a grip handle in the bottom-right corner drags the dialog's width/height (tracked in local `useState`, clamped to `UI.POD_DETAILS_WIDTH_MIN/MAX` and `..._HEIGHT_MIN/MAX` in `shared/constants`), following the same delta-from-drag-start approach as the sidebar resize in `App.tsx` but scoped locally to the component instead of lifted to app state — the size only matters while the overlay is open and has no other consumer. The dialog switched from content-sized (`max-w-lg`/`max-h-[60vh]`) to an explicit `flex flex-col` layout with a `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto` body so the fixed pixel size still scrolls correctly at any dimension.
 - Status/ready badges ("Running", "Ready") use a `--k8s-success` CSS variable (`text-k8s-success`/`bg-k8s-success/15`, registered in the `@theme` block in `index.css`) instead of Tailwind's fixed `green-400`/`green-500`. `green-400` (`#4ade80`) reads fine against the dark and darcula themes' near-black backgrounds but fails contrast against the light theme's pale background (`#f0f4f8`), so `:root` (light) defines `--k8s-success: #15803d` (a much darker green) while `.dark`/`.darcula` keep `#4ade80`. This mirrors how every other themed color (`k8s-link`, `k8s-muted`, etc.) is defined per-theme in `index.css` rather than hardcoding a Tailwind palette color that ignores the active theme.
+- `CustomSelect` (`features/ui/components/`) gained an opt-in `filterable`/`filterPlaceholder` prop pair: when set, an auto-focused text input renders above the option list and filters options by a case-insensitive substring match on `label`. `ContextSelector` and `NamespaceSelector` pass `filterable` (context/namespace lists can grow long); `ThemeSelector`'s fixed four-option list leaves it off (the default), so that consumer is unaffected. The option list also gained a `max-h-60 overflow-y-auto` cap so a long (filtered or unfiltered) list no longer grows the dropdown past the viewport. The filter query resets whenever the dropdown closes, so each open starts from a clean slate.
 
 ## Performance Optimizations
 
